 "drivingQuestion": "Why is one suspect on tithes not suspect on shevi'it?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "bekhorot.30a.5",
   "daf": "30a",
   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "הֶחָשׁוּד עַל הַמַּעֲשֵׂר. מַאי טַעְמָא? מַעֲשֵׂר אִית לֵיהּ פִּדְיוֹן, שְׁבִיעִית — כֵּיוָן דְּקָא מִיתַּסְרָא לֵיהּ וְלֵית לֵיהּ פִּדְיוֹן — חֲמִירָא לֵיהּ.",
   "en": "The mishna teaches: «One who is suspect with regard to tithe» is not suspect with regard to the Sabbatical Year. The Gemara asks: «What is the reason?» The Gemara answers: Since «there is redemption» for «tithes,» one might treat them lightly. As for produce of the «Sabbatical» Year, «since it is» always «prohibited to him and there is no redemption» of it, it is possible that it seems more «stringent for him,» and therefore he is not suspect."
  }
 ],
